1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,720
Structural patterns assembled objects.
Behavioral patterns organize algorithms
and communication — how work varies, how
events propagate, how requests become
objects.

2
00:00:09,839 --> 00:00:22,160
If creational is birth and structural is
anatomy, behavioral is choreography. Start
with a deep conditional that everyone
regrets: Look at this java for a moment.
Every new promotion type edits this spine.

3
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:30,920
Strategy replaces it with a common
interface and swappable implementations.
The caller depends on DiscountPolicy, not
on a growing if tower.

4
00:00:31,039 --> 00:00:41,920
Strategy essence: swap algorithms behind a
common interface without rewriting
callers. The failure mode is Strategy
interfaces with one implementation forever
— pure ceremony.

5
00:00:42,039 --> 00:00:53,960
Use Strategy when variation is real and
expected to grow. Keep a simple switch
when few stable variants live local and no
extension is expected. Admitting the non-
pattern choice is part of pattern
literacy.

6
00:00:54,079 --> 00:01:02,280
A DiscountPolicy functional interface can
be implemented by classes or lambdas. The
important part is the seam: checkout
depends on the interface.

7
00:01:02,399 --> 00:01:15,920
Unit tests inject a fixed policy;
production wires seasonal policies from
configuration. The pattern is the seam,
not the ceremony of anonymous inner
classes from 2005. Observer fits events.

8
00:01:16,039 --> 00:01:26,519
Something interesting happens — order
placed, user registered — and multiple
listeners react. The subject notifies
observers without hard-coding each
reaction. Useful.

9
00:01:26,639 --> 00:01:36,319
Also leaky: forgotten observers are the
listener leaks from Episode Fifty-Seven
wearing a pattern name. Register and
unregister with clear lifetimes.

10
00:01:36,439 --> 00:01:46,479
A component that registers on a long-lived
bus and is never removed keeps its graph
alive; heaps climb. The pattern did not
cause the leak — unbounded lifetime did.

11
00:01:46,599 --> 00:01:57,159
In modern systems, message buses play
Observer at a larger scale, with the same
lifetime discipline — plus at-least-once
delivery and idempotency that later
episodes treat seriously.

12
00:01:57,279 --> 00:02:02,879
Template Method uses inheritance to fix an
algorithm skeleton while subclasses fill
steps.

13
00:02:02,999 --> 00:02:14,399
Composition with Strategy-like hooks often
ages better in Java than deep template
hierarchies, but you will still meet
Template Method in frameworks — learn the
hooks rather than fighting the skeleton.

14
00:02:14,519 --> 00:02:30,199
Command turns a request into an object —
useful for queues, undo stacks, and audit
trails. RefundOrder carries the data
needed to perform and to record. Retries
become re-execution; undo becomes a
compensating command.

15
00:02:30,319 --> 00:02:42,479
If you never retry, never audit, and never
undo, a method call may suffice. Command
explosion without need is busywork. Walk a
checkout flow. Pricing uses Strategy for
discount policies.

16
00:02:42,599 --> 00:02:51,240
Placing an order publishes an event; email
and inventory observe. A Command
representing "cancel order" sits on an
admin undo stack.

17
00:02:51,359 --> 00:03:03,879
Each pattern appears because a problem
appeared — not because a chapter checklist
demanded coverage. That necessity test is
the same one Episode Sixty-Seven taught.
Behavioral patterns also meet concurrency.

18
00:03:03,999 --> 00:03:13,799
Strategy objects should usually be
stateless or immutable so they can be
shared across threads. Observers that
mutate shared collections need the
discipline from the concurrency arc.

19
00:03:13,919 --> 00:03:27,159
Commands on queues must be serializable or
mappable if they cross process boundaries.
The pattern sketch is single-threaded;
production choreography is not. Do not
over-abstract one-off code.

20
00:03:27,279 --> 00:03:38,359
Behavioral patterns shine when
communication or algorithm variation is a
recurring pain. They dull when every
method becomes an interface hierarchy "for
testing" without a second implementation
in sight.

21
00:03:38,479 --> 00:03:50,359
Prefer the smallest structure that keeps
change local. Interviewers who ask for a
behavioral pattern you used want a story:
we replaced a switch with Strategy because
marketing added three discount types in a
quarter.

22
00:03:50,479 --> 00:03:55,399
Mechanisms plus timeline beat trivia.
Behavioral patterns close the classical
catalog arc.

23
00:03:55,519 --> 00:04:08,559
Next we enter the ecosystem where many of
these ideas are industrialized for
enterprise Java: Spring — dependency
injection, portable abstractions, and a
container mindset — starting from a
practical situation,

24
00:04:08,679 --> 00:04:10,279
not a feature brochure.
